SUMMARY:VotingMatters by Abridged by PBS KVIE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T193000
UID:a16cb5d4e6f25c11fa06b0abb56fc7f8@events.yolocountylibrary.org
DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about the election? Where do the governo
 r candidates stand on the issues? What does the insurance commissioner do?
 \n\nPlease join us on May 22 as we welcome the nonprofit statewide publica
 tion CalMatters as they break down\, analyze and answer your burning que
 stions about this year’s primary election\, in a conversation centered a
 round the latest edition of their Voter Guide.\n\nFeatured guests include 
 Abridged by PBS KVIE’s Yolo County reporter Daniel Hennessy and Executiv
 e Director of Davis Media Access Autumn Labbe-Renault.\n\nThe local iterat
 ion of this event is sponsored by the Yolo County Library.\n\n\n	Doors ope
 n at 5:30PM\n	Introduction\, trivia\, local partners speak\, main portion 
 to discuss issues\, closing\n	Tickets are free\, but seating is limited\n	
 The event will be held from 6 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. on Friday\, May 22\, insid
 e the Blanchard Room at the Mary L. Stephens-Davis Branch Library.\n	Food 
 will be provided by CalMatters\n\n\nBy reserving a ticket\, you agree to r
 eceive occasional marketing updates from Abridged by PBS KVIE.\n\nReserve 
 your ticket here: Eventbrite
LOCATION:Blanchard Room\, Small Conference Room\, Mary L Stephens Davis Br
 anch Library
URL:https://events.yolocountylibrary.org/event/16878552
X-SOURCE:Yolo Library
END:VEVENT
